{
  "_comment": [
    "Plaid sandbox custom-user config: the statement the demo reads.",
    "",
    "Plaid's stock test institution returns five merchants repeated monthly,",
    "twelve of them at exactly $500 -- a $500 order at KFC among them. The",
    "figures Pointwise derives from that are arithmetically right and read as",
    "nonsense, which costs the whole screen its credibility. This replaces it.",
    "",
    "Two rules shaped the merchant list. Most names are ones the merchant map",
    "in category_tables.py already holds a real MCC for, so they resolve at",
    "'known' confidence rather than leaning on the aggregator. A few are not,",
    "on purpose: Zuni Cafe and Tartine resolve by keyword and the row says so",
    "in italics. A demo that never shows the app admitting a guess hides the",
    "part of the design worth showing.",
    "",
    "Plaid enriches these: it returns a personal_finance_category for each row",
    "even though the config has no category field, and it rewrites some names",
    "(Whole Foods Market -> Whole Foods). It returns no merchant_name, so the",
    "description below is what the app matches on.",
    "",
    "Amounts are positive, which is how Plaid reports a card purchase.",
    "Regenerate with: PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python scripts/seed_plaid_demo.py"
  ],
